            <ArticleTitle>Impact of different anatomical patterns of left main coronary stenting on long-term survival.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>718-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There are no significant differences in long-term and event-free survival in patients who undergo stent implantation in different anatomic locations of the left main coronary artery. Predictors of long-term survival are age &lt;65 years, normal left ventricular ejection fraction, and absence of an intra-aortic balloon pump.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
